ble 3</xref> <table-wrap id="tbl3" position="float"><label>Table 3</label><caption><p content-type="table-title">Relative risk (RR) of prostate cancer from the Cox regression analysis with 95&#x00025; confidence intervals (CI) by age at measurement and body mass index (BMI) or height, adjusted for birth cohort</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups" border="1" width="85%"><colgroup><col align="left"/><col align="left"/><col align="left"/><col align="left"/><col align="left"/><col align="left"/><col align="left"/><col align="left"/><col align="left"/><col align="left"/><col align="left"/><col align="left"/><col align="left"/></colgroup><thead valign="bottom"><tr><th align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">&#x000a0;</th><th colspan="12" align="center" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold>Age at measurement (years)</bold><hr/></th></tr><tr><th align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">&#x000a0;</th><th colspan="2" align="center" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold>20&#x02013;29 (622 cases)</bold><hr/></th><th colspan="2" align="center" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold>30&#x02013;39 (3196 cases)</bold><hr/></th><th colspan="2" align="center" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold>40&#x02013;49 (8996 cases)</bold><hr/></th><th colspan="2" align="center" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold>50&#x02013;59 (11&#x02009;009 cases)</bold><hr/></th><th colspan="2" align="center" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold>60&#x02013;69 (7594 cases)</bold><hr/></th><th colspan="2" align="center" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold>70&#x02013;74 (1897 cases)</bold><hr/></th></tr><tr><th align="left" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold>Variable</bold></th><th align="left" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold>RR</bold></th><th align="left" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold>95&#x00025; CI</bold></th><th align="left" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold>RR</bold></th><th align="left" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold>95&#x00025; CI</bold></th><th align="left" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold>RR</bold></th><th align="left" valign="top